  m_Name: FirstCamp
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuestDefinition
  id: firstcamp
  displayName: A Light in the Wood
  description: The forest cannot forget a hearth that someone tends. An ember from the shelter's fire came through the catch with you, still alive. Set it in the cold hearth in front of the portal, inside its ward. Your people will see it through the mist.
  chain: The Hearth and the Door
  journalNotes: 'This is the old bargain, though you are only starting to understand it. A fire inside the ward feeds the ward. It also shows, a long way off, to anyone who is looking for it.


    You kept their fire: the ember from the shelter. The cold hearth by the portal takes it ({key:Interact}). Any campfire you build inside the ward counts too.'
